detailedExplanation.whatItIs:
Top-N-per-group is the problem of returning, say, the 3 highest-paid employees in each department or the latest order per customer. The canonical solution numbers or ranks rows within each partition and filters by that number. Example:
SELECT * FROM (
  SELECT *, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY dept ORDER BY salary DESC) rn
  FROM employees
) t WHERE rn <= 3;
